# Line-ending policy
# ------------------
# The index stores every text file with LF. `eol=lf` makes checkouts write LF
# on every platform, so Windows working trees match what Flutter tooling
# writes (it always emits LF) and files stop flip-flopping between
# "modified" and clean under core.autocrlf=true.
# `text=auto` still lets Git auto-detect and skip truly binary files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary protection (belt-and-braces beside auto-detection).
*.png binary
*.ico binary

# Windows scripts keep CRLF; cmd.exe and older PowerShell expect it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
